      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1000 mg per dose. Overdosing raises the risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day) is the maximum dose.\n- **1000 mg twice daily** (2,000 mg/day) is a common regimen.\n- **1700 mg total per day**, split into doses such as 850 mg twice daily.\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose and frequency, and I'll enter the order right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical reason. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
