       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. A dose of 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and I know of no clinical indication that justifies it. It could cause serious harm, such as lactic acidosis, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some other ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can do that now, for example 850 mg three times daily or 1000 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **Call pharmacy or the attending.** If you think this dose is intended, they can review it and enter it through a pathway with a documented override.\n- **Check for a transcription error.** The dose may have been mistyped or misread from another source.\n\nIf you tell me which dose you want, I'll enter it."
